N5008 [dcl.init.aggr]/1: a user-declared constructor template (not stored as a
struct component; the type carries `has_template_constructor`) makes the class
a non-aggregate, so `ref<int[5]> r{arr}` / `ref{arr}` call the forwarding
constructor instead of aggregate-initialising the pointer member from the
array (libstdc++ ranges::ref_view).  Three call sites checked: the local
declaration path, the explicit-constructor-call path and the braced-temporary
path.  Non-vacuous: the last assertion states a wrong value and must FAIL.
